mes as its own (_queue.SimpleQueue, _random.Random) is that module's, not a"] [147 3 "// builtin (queue 595: a subinterpreter's exec() globals' __builtins__ pickled back, test_interpreters'"] [148 3 "// test_modified_arg)"] [159 62 "// builtins' one underscored type (PY7)"] [165 55 "// PY6a, by the integration's owner (test_grammar); -O (py-os-1124)"] [174 1 "// readyTypes completes every registered type once, after every file's init has set its slots"] [175 1 "// (CPython's PyType_Ready): bases, MRO, and the slots a type leaves nil inherited from its base."] [193 2 "// type_ready's type_dict_set_doc: a static type's dict always holds __doc__, its tp_doc or None (pyi has no C"] [194 2 "// docstrings yet: None), so an instance's __doc__ is found (\"abc\".__doc__ raised AttributeError; email's"] [195 2 "// _policybase reads attr.__doc__ of every class attribute); not where the type or a base answers __doc__ by a"] [196 2 "// getset (pyi's getsets are outside the dict: property's settable __doc__ would be shadowed)"] [199 33 "// CPython's tp_doc less its signature (py-core-1124)"] [208 1 "// docGetSet reports whether a type of t's MRO has a __doc__ getset."] [231 1 "// inheritSlots fills s's nil slots from b's (CPython's inherit_slots)."] [330 1 "// ownSlots are the special methods a built-in type defines itself, before inheritSlots fills the rest:"] [331 1 "// its __dict__ lists their slot wrappers, as CPython's does (enum's _find_data_type_ asks"] [332 1 "// '__new__' in int.__dict__). Added by PY5e as the integration's owner (part 2b)."] [349 2 "// add_operators: the number protocol's and the comparisons' wrappers (PY6e's REQUEST d27906db)"] [374 1 "// slottedName: the special methods recordOwnSlots records; ownsSlot is built-in type m showing name's wrapper in"] [375 1 "// its own __dict__: a subclass inherits the slot, so that bool.__add__ is int.__add__ as in CPython."] [383 1 "// inheritsNew are the built-in types whose tp_new is their base's (queue 545: _io's types but FileIO, BytesIO and"] [384 1 "// StringIO): no __new__ of their own, though their Slots.New makes their value."] [404 3 "// \"r\"+d and \"i\"+d compared without making them (queue 305: a concatenation per name, 5% of an import's start)"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[38 40] [199 26]] :go/trails [[139 25]]} (go/file "registry.go" :imports [])

;; The registry of built-in types and functions (doc/python/PYI-SPEC.md §7.3): each file of the runtime
;; declares its types as package variables made by NewBuiltinType (no slots: slots are set in the file's
;; init function, after every type exists, so the slots' functions may name any type) and registers
;; its built-in functions with RegisterBuiltin. The builtins module of an Interp is made from the
;; registry: every registered type and function whose name is public, in registration order.

